{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions","id":1535340,"title":"W5 videogame/text-adventure \"Book Of Hungry Names\" - Review/First Impressions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-09T05:03:51-07:00","id":1535340,"title":"W5 videogame/text-adventure \"Book Of Hungry Names\" - Review/First Impressions","content":"So, the bad news first... I nearly finished the game but then a recent patch nuked the save, so now I have to start all over again... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I think I can at least offer some impressions of that first run and how the setting and the characters are portrayed.<ul><li>Setting/Lore: Like the supplements from Renegade, the descriptions of the setting couldn't remain as unspecific as the corebook but I also don't think this is the exact same take on the W5 corebook as the Renegade-supplements' and it also doesn't stay wholly true to what's laid out in the corebook. It's a setting where the Pack is the most complex level of social organisation left and there are various Garou around who don't even have a Pack but act independently instead. There's a Sept/caern which is part of the main-story but it's a fallen one. The Umbra is dangerous although not because Garou can't survive in it but because all the spirits either are corrupted by the Wyrm, want nothing to do with Garou, are angry at Garou for the state of the world or the Spirits in question have just gone insane since the Gaia's Howl event. Or for example, since I chose a Silver Fang, one Garou mentions that in this continuity this Garou heard of this rumor that the last Silver Fang with prominent ancestry died in the early 90s in Russia and since then the standards for joining the Silver Fangs have been loosened. That's already more lore than what you get from the corebook. Oh, also you meet a Drone in the story (the Weaver-equivalent of a Fomor). Something else the W5 corebook didn't adequately cover.</li> <li>Tribes: The way it's portrayed it really is more about describing a Garou who has made a pact with a particular Tribe-Patron-Spirit. And because of the sort of people who can make a Pact with a certain Patron-Spirit, stereotypes for these Tribes emerge. But it's not like the Tribe is treated like some sort of other social organisation within the Garou Nation. But the game also mentions Patron-Spirits at the heart of caerns (which the corebook doesn't really cover despite having this caern-management-system) and there's talk of Pack-guardian-spirits (in other words, Pack-Patron-Spirits).</li> <li>Themes: What I appreciate about the game is that it certainly has a more nuanced take on the W5 themes than the W5 corebook has. You still have the Age of Apocalypse and the fallen Garou-Nation but the focus is much more on charting a new course and what that new course looks like. For that reason, you get these trackers with opposing ideas of what the new priorities are.</li> <li>It goes like this: &quot;The Litany has failed - Rebuild the Litany&quot;, &quot;Humans must pay - Humans must understand&quot;, &quot;Our weapon is Rage - Our Answer is Spirit&quot;, &quot;I Just Want to Survive - We can still win&quot;, &quot;Find purpose through dignity - Find courage through laughter.&quot;. If you were to take a look at the W5 corebook, the authors kinda have made up their minds already on some of those matters without leaving it to the people at the table to decide how to approach these things.</li> <li>Garou-characterization: In my first playthrough, I focused on building connections with the Garou and ignore the humans and I gotta say... horrible decision. There isn't a single Garou I would call likeable. The main-issue is that this game really hammers home just how debilitating the whole Rage-thing is. These Garou are always super-combative with each other and ready to start arguments at nearly every opportunity. Especially the Pack you start out with... Man, what a bunch of assholes. The game starts with you killing some Wyrm-spawn but then it turns out that it was just some riding-animal for a Fomor or something and the Garou-Elders in your Pack immediately mock your killing and declare that since it was the mount it doesn't count. That's the other thing: The whole Elder-thing is often used by Garou to lord that over younger Garou. But Elder also just means a Garou who's older than you. So there's situations where one Garou-character acts like an Elder-asshole to you but then when an even older Garou shows up they then act like an asshole to the Garou who was just being an asshole to you.</li> <li>But also that initial Pack are such assholes because the leader of that Pack additionally starts eating the Wyrmspawn and talks about how the Litany is a waste of time. And then he immediately gets sick and starts dying. I mean... hell of a way to introduce W5 Garou...</li> <li>Cult of Fenris: So they're described as Nazis but it also a bit confused because it's described that one of the Fenrir was wearing a Vegan Reich shirt. It felt more like this hodgepodge of all kinds of different kinds of conservative extremism. What the dialogue focused on more, though, was the Fenrir talking about how they're the true Garou Nation and all the other Garou are too weak to get the job done. But the politics were there more as aesthetics. Well, it all felt a bit weird. Like in one instance where one Garou said &quot;You know, I'm not one of those Garou who's racist towards Bone Gnawers.&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T06:55:57-07:00","id":1535345,"title":"","content":"So, basically most garou are just doing whatever, the Fenrir are Conservative and Gaia's Howl is a thing.<br /> <br /> Does the setting feels like something you could play in, compared to W5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T08:08:12-07:00","id":1535349,"title":"","content":"Yeah it does. I started playing and BoHN is at least not giving you the feeling of being another Stealth Werewolf The Forsaken unlike W5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T09:57:35-07:00","id":1535358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535345#post1535345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, basically most garou are just doing whatever, the Fenrir are Conservative and Gaia's Howl is a thing.<br /> <br /> Does the setting feels like something you could play in, compared to W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting feels better than the one outlined in the W5 corebook. And it feels more substantive as well. But in its street-level-only outlook, I really couldn't help but think that WtF has the better premise for that sort of thing. So, the essential structure is that you start with this Pack of Garou who are assholes and they fuck up. You go looking for help and that's how you stumble into this bigger story-arc of reawakening a fallen caern. But you're also collecting members for your own/a new Pack along the way. That's the story-structure. And one of these instances is about a harvesting-spirit (that has gone insane because of Gaia's Howl) holding a rural town hostage which has become a weird cult. And one of the Garou has been caught up in this. But all I could think about was that this would work better as a WtF-premise. You're better off doing that in WtF than in WtA.<br /> <br /> There's also a similar issue I have with H5: The horizon is just so limited. Okay, you restored the Sept/caern and... now what? W5 has no answer for you on that front. The same way that anything beyond being a local hunter-cell is unimaginable in H5. Because the issue is that all this stuff in the setting got torn down in H5 and W5 but it doesn't feel like these two corebooks imagine any players successfully rebuilding stuff or go beyond the limitations of their origins. &quot;It's the Age of Apocalypse - but remember that the world is already doomed to die.&quot; or &quot;It's the Age of Reckoning - but remember that any gathering of mortal hunters who want to kill supernatural monsters that goes beyond a local hunter-cell is corrupt and fundamentally bad.&quot;. Neither game is very good at justifying the outlined struggle of prospective PCs within the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T10:49:32-07:00","id":1535361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions#post1535340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or for example, since I chose a Silver Fang, one Garou mentions that in this continuity this Garou heard of this rumor that the last Silver Fang with prominent ancestry died in the early 90s in Russia</div> </div> </div> </div>[Really nasty eye twitch]<br /> <br /> [EXTERNAL SCREAMING!]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T14:42:23-07:00","id":1535374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535361#post1535361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [Really nasty eye twitch]<br /> <br /> [EXTERNAL SCREAMING!]</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair shartted nation basically contradict that since the book did mention an Albrecht linage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T18:56:33-07:00","id":1535393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535374#post1535374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair shartted nation basically contradict that since the book did mention an Albrecht linage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I immediately thought of that as well. You can't do &quot;The Return of King Albrecht&quot; with that conception of the Silver Fang Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-09T20:14:03-07:00","id":1535397,"title":"","content":"There's a ton of lore and history dropped in this gamebook that isn't&quot;t in the core or Renegade releases.....is it canon or &quot;canon&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T00:22:20-07:00","id":1535404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535358#post1535358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also a similar issue I have with H5: The horizon is just so limited. Okay, you restored the Sept/caern and... now what? W5 has no answer for you on that front. The same way that anything beyond being a local hunter-cell is unimaginable in H5. Because the issue is that all this stuff in the setting got torn down in H5 and W5 but it doesn't feel like these two corebooks imagine any players successfully rebuilding stuff or go beyond the limitations of their origins. &quot;It's the Age of Apocalypse - but remember that the world is already doomed to die.&quot; or &quot;It's the Age of Reckoning - but remember that any gathering of mortal hunters who want to kill supernatural monsters that goes beyond a local hunter-cell is corrupt and fundamentally bad.&quot;. Neither game is very good at justifying the outlined struggle of prospective PCs within the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember how, before W5 came out, I pondered how long these games were meant to be? I am still asking the same question as it seems the goal ends with a Caern and then the game becomes Caern Tending Simulation with no end.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-10T20:49:20-07:00","id":1535429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535397#post1535397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a ton of lore and history dropped in this gamebook that isn't&quot;t in the core or Renegade releases.....is it canon or &quot;canon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>To make things more confusing <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> one of the endings involves ressurcting all of the MC's former pack's anstor spirts, who basically, plan on going around the world to help other packs in need and genially attempt spread a sense of unity amoung the garou.</div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> This is qute a massive shake up to the metaplot leave in a CYOA book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T00:34:54-07:00","id":1535431,"title":"","content":"Ancestor spirits are also mentioned in a recent Renegade adventure. And while they used to be a thing, the tricky thing is that the W5 corebook never mentioned them. And you couldn't do that line from the corebook that nobody knows for how long the Garou Nation even lasted, for example, if Ancestor spirits are a thing again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T00:40:00-07:00","id":1535432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535431#post1535431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancestor spirits are also mentioned in a recent Renegade adventure. And while they used to be a thing, the tricky thing is that the W5 corebook never mentioned them. And you couldn't do that line from the corebook that nobody knows for how long the Garou Nation even lasted, for example, if Ancestor spirits are a thing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I legit think they need to release a new core very soon. If your 're-imagening' needs people to look at older editions for context? It has failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T12:08:49-07:00","id":1535452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535431#post1535431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancestor spirits are also mentioned in a recent Renegade adventure. And while they used to be a thing, the tricky thing is that the W5 corebook never mentioned them. And you couldn't do that line from the corebook that nobody knows for how long the Garou Nation even lasted, for example, if Ancestor spirits are a thing again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technicality!<br /> <br /> They are mentioned precisely once in the Corebook. on page 235:<br /> <br /> &quot;Jagglings, among all spirits, are the ones werewolves are perhaps most, and most frequently, familiar with. The animal-spirits that teach Garou gifts, the Banes whose cruel possessions they fight, and the ancestor-spirits that inhabit their Caerns.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course they're not mentioned in the Caerns section.......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-11T12:51:04-07:00","id":1535456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535397#post1535397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a ton of lore and history dropped in this gamebook that isn't&quot;t in the core or Renegade releases.....is it canon or &quot;canon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're going to use that same explanation from Earthblood. Partially canonical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T12:25:01-07:00","id":1535660,"title":"","content":"A few points I would like to make in regards to this:<ul><li>Clay doesn't mock the Litany when eating the Fomori at the start of the game, <b>you</b> do. He claims &quot;The First Share of the Kill For the Greatest in Station&quot; at which point your Garou goes &quot;That probably was applicable back during hunter-gatherer days but what the fuck does that matter now?&quot; Clay gets poisoned because he is strictly adhering to the Litany without thought. Cuz y'know, Elder.</li> <li>W5 does mention patron spirits of Caerns on page 194. It doesn't specifically mention they need to Tribal-related, because they don't, but there's no reason you couldn't have them be an aspect of a larger Incarnae. Likewise Pack Patrons can be done through the Rite of Patronage just 10 pages before. Considering the Patronage bonuses are all 1-die and a Ban, they are perhaps the easiest thing in the world to Homebrew if you'd want to.</li> <li>In regards to: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It goes like this: &quot;The Litany has failed - Rebuild the Litany&quot;, &quot;Humans must pay - Humans must understand&quot;, &quot;Our weapon is Rage - Our Answer is Spirit&quot;, &quot;I Just Want to Survive - We can still win&quot;, &quot;Find purpose through dignity - Find courage through laughter.&quot;. If you were to take a look at the W5 corebook, the authors kinda have made up their minds already on some of those matters without leaving it to the people at the table to decide how to approach these things. </div> </div> </div></li> <li>Most of these are just Chronicle Tenants and a lot of them are just example ones from W5, or related to it's stated themes. These are definitely covered and supported by the book.</li> <li>Your starting pack being assholes Is The Point yeah. They're old bastards lamenting that they lost and all their old glories are gone to the past and taking it out on you by proxy. There's a reason your new pack reacts to them by going &quot;hey fuck this guy&quot;. Though I had a pretty interesting mentor/student relationship with Black Tarn as a Theurge.</li> <li>I personally can't agree on the new pack being unlikable. Elton, Podge, Melodie, and Nim were all incredibly charming to me. Like yeah they argue and get heated about it which has been a core Garou thing since I believe the inception of Garou as a Thing. But it's not like there's debilitating infighting, just ideological disagreements. Everyone still works together and obviously likes each other.</li> <li>For the record I did what you did too, I played a Silver Fang Theurge with a focus on maxing my Honor out as much as possible and a character focused mainly on rebuilding a New Nation. It was an incredibly satisfying playstyle and I'm really glad I went through it to the end, even if I'm a bit mad that I couldn't replicate a decision I made due to the aforementioned auto-save glitch (which according to patch notes is now fixed! Yipee).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T13:42:41-07:00","id":1535673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535660#post1535660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few points I would like to make in regards to this:<br /> Clay doesn't mock the Litany when eating the Fomori at the start of the game, <b>you</b> do. He claims &quot;The First Share of the Kill For the Greatest in Station&quot; at which point your Garou goes &quot;That probably was applicable back during hunter-gatherer days but what the fuck does that matter now?&quot; Clay gets poisoned because he is strictly adhering to the Litany without thought. Cuz y'know, Elder.</div> </div> </div> </div>When did you play the game? Because I noticed that as well on my second playthrough. That has changed. Because the first time I played it there were options and I picked the one where I reprimanded Clay for disobeying the Litany during that opening. And that moment wasn't there during the second playthrough. That opening-bit was much longer the first time I played it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> W5 does mention patron spirits of Caerns on page 194. It doesn't specifically mention they need to Tribal-related, because they don't, but there's no reason you couldn't have them be an aspect of a larger Incarnae. Likewise Pack Patrons can be done through the Rite of Patronage just 10 pages before. Considering the Patronage bonuses are all 1-die and a Ban, they are perhaps the easiest thing in the world to Homebrew if you'd want to. </div> </div> </div>Well, it's way more complicated than that. One, Favors and Bans are inconsistent. There are three different types of Favors in the W5 corebook (version one is just a list of Skills, version 2 is skills under specific circumstances and version 3 is just a specific circumstance) and the Bans have some wild swings in their &quot;If you do this...&quot;-scenarios with some Tribe-Bans being way more punishing than others.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the referenced Rite only refers to Tribe-Patron-Spirits.<br /> <br /> And so overall, it is a bit of a challenge to houserule this if you want to stay consistent with the W5 corebook. Then again, the actual issue is that the W5 corebook itself isn't consistent. In the past, I mentioned in another thread that for the sake of homebrewing it would be sensible to give up on the inconsistent semantics-game from the W5 corebook and instead just opt to replace Tribe-Favors with a suitable free Skill-Specialization. You still get the bonus-die but without the hang-ups of the inconsistencies you find in the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of these are just Chronicle Tenants and a lot of them are just example ones from W5, or related to it's stated themes. These are definitely covered and supported by the book. </div> </div> </div>That's a very generous reading in my opinion. For those who don't have the W5 corebook, here are the proposed Chronicle Tenets in the W5 corebook (pg 200):<br /> <br /> Environmentalist<ul><li>Never cause harm to Gaia</li> <li>Do not hoard resources</li> <li>Never put short-term gains ahead of long-term goals</li> </ul>Apocalypse Radicalism<ul><li>Do not cling to the old ways</li> <li>Never kill an outsider</li> <li>Vengeance must be served\u200b</li> </ul>Traditionalist<ul><li>Uphold the Litany</li> <li>Heed your elders</li> <li>Only ritual challenge merits killing of other Garou\u200b</li> </ul><br /> And of course that has to be seen in the context of a book that has lines like &quot;For all of the self-glorifying tales that old Garou tell around the fires, younger werewolves note that the Garou Nation didn\u2019t collapse because the Litany was so goddamn perfect.&quot; (pg 47) or &quot;The Garou are built to act, but they\u2019re probably too late. Worse, the resources they have aren\u2019t what they need.\u200b&quot; (pg 202). The latter quote is made worse by W5 still being a game about Garou doing Garou-stuff. The &quot;Garou have to reinvent/reform themselves&quot;-part isn't supported one bit but instead it's just called out as a thing that has to happen. Instead, the W5 corebook <i>assumes </i>W5 players will end up managing a caern at some point (pg 191). And that the game really is all about &quot;small victories&quot;. That's what you get from the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Also, please don't be too hard on corporations... That's another piece of advice you get from the W5 corebook (pg 26).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your starting pack being assholes Is The Point yeah. They're old bastards lamenting that they lost and all their old glories are gone to the past and taking it out on you by proxy. There's a reason your new pack reacts to them by going &quot;hey fuck this guy&quot;. Though I had a pretty interesting mentor/student relationship with Black Tarn as a Theurge. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get that that's the point but I don't like it. Seems a bit counter-intuitive to me to start introductions by telling players/readers that Garou can be real assholes sometimes. I played an Ahroun for the first playthrough so I didn't try to rescue Black Tarn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally can't agree on the new pack being unlikable. Elton, Podge, Melodie, and Nim were all incredibly charming to me. Like yeah they argue and get heated about it which has been a core Garou thing since I believe the inception of Garou as a Thing. But it's not like there's debilitating infighting, just ideological disagreements. Everyone still works together and obviously likes each other. </div> </div> </div>Well, that's personal taste, I guess... I didn't like any of them. Usually with these sorts of setups where you have multiple companions and part of the story-structure is to pick them up, make them part of your &quot;squad&quot; and do &quot;Loyalty-missions&quot;, characters emerge that I find more likable than others but that weren't the situation here. I didn't like any of them. None of them seemed interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T14:23:15-07:00","id":1535675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535673#post1535673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When did you play the game? Because I noticed that as well on my second playthrough. That has changed. Because the first time I played it there were options and I picked the one where I reprimanded Clay for disobeying the Litany during that opening. And that moment wasn't there during the second playthrough. That opening-bit was much longer the first time I played it.</div> </div> </div> </div>On launch. Don't remember my dialogue choice but I do remember getting that response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535673#post1535673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's way more complicated than that. One, Favors and Bans are inconsistent. There are three different types of Favors in the W5 corebook (version one is just a list of Skills, version 2 is skills under specific circumstances and version 3 is just a specific circumstance) and the Bans have some wild swings in their &quot;If you do this...&quot;-scenarios with some Tribe-Bans being way more punishing than others.<br /> <br /> Additionally, the referenced Rite only refers to Tribe-Patron-Spirits.<br /> <br /> And so overall, it is a bit of a challenge to houserule this if you want to stay consistent with the W5 corebook. Then again, the actual issue is that the W5 corebook itself isn't consistent. In the past, I mentioned in another thread that for the sake of homebrewing it would be sensible to give up on the inconsistent semantics-game from the W5 corebook and instead just opt to replace Tribe-Favors with a suitable free Skill-Specialization. You still get the bonus-die but without the hang-ups of the inconsistencies you find in the W5 corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that's probably a good way to Homebrew it. But if if you're doing a pack-patron where everyone's getting the same general Favour and Ban, then it's not really &quot;unbalanced&quot; or anything, you're just putting stock into what your Chronicle is going to be about specifically. Everyone has the same access to it and is punished the same way, rather than things being all over the place. So homebrewing doesn't really have to worry about &quot;imbalance&quot; because every PC gets the same buff and punishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535673#post1535673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a very generous reading in my opinion. For those who don't have the W5 corebook, here are the proposed Chronicle Tenets in the W5 corebook (pg 200):<br /> <br /> Environmentalist<ul><li>Never cause harm to Gaia</li> <li>Do not hoard resources</li> <li>Never put short-term gains ahead of long-term goals</li> </ul>Apocalypse Radicalism<ul><li>Do not cling to the old ways</li> <li>Never kill an outsider</li> <li>Vengeance must be served</li> </ul>Traditionalist<ul><li>Uphold the Litany</li> <li>Heed your elders</li> <li>Only ritual challenge merits killing of other Garou\u200b</li> </ul><br /> And of course that has to be seen in the context of a book that has lines like &quot;For all of the self-glorifying tales that old Garou tell around the fires, younger werewolves note that the Garou Nation didn\u2019t collapse because the Litany was so goddamn perfect.&quot; (pg 47) or &quot;The Garou are built to act, but they\u2019re probably too late. Worse, the resources they have aren\u2019t what they need.\u200b&quot; (pg 202). The latter quote is made worse by W5 still being a game about Garou doing Garou-stuff. The &quot;Garou have to reinvent/reform themselves&quot;-part isn't supported one bit but instead it's just called out as a thing that has to happen. Instead, the W5 corebook <i>assumes </i>W5 players will end up managing a caern at some point (pg 191). And that the game really is all about &quot;small victories&quot;. That's what you get from the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> Also, please don't be too hard on corporations... That's another piece of advice you get from the W5 corebook (pg 26).</div> </div> </div> </div>For one, younger Garou thinking the Litany is bullshit and that the Elders are talking nonsense (and are indeed part of the problem) isn't a W5 thing. It's an Apocalypse thing in general, and as far as I can tell has been a running theme for most of it. Likewise, the entire mood of older editions was saying that the Apocalypse is here, you're too late, and there's nothing you can do to avert it. This isn't a new addition to W5 either. I think W5 is actually <b>more</b> hopeful with it's tone by having Gaia be dead and the Apocalypse already ongoing or over, tbh. (A whole thing which I will probably have to put into it's own post.)<br /> <br /> The Garou having to relearn themselves is I think reflected pretty well in tone and showcased really well in BoHN. You're a creature of violence with a bubbling Rage underneath the surface, now try to make your community better and maintain your human connections. Like BoHN showcases this really well I think, with each Garou you meet being a weird iconoclast in some way shape or form. It's everyone scrounging to rebuild in the way they see fit in the midst of overwhelming trauma and grief.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535673#post1535673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get that that's the point but I don't like it. Seems a bit counter-intuitive to me to start introductions by telling players/readers that Garou can be real assholes sometimes. I played an Ahroun for the first playthrough so I didn't try to rescue Black Tarn.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> I mean it's establishing where you're starting from. You're a kid from an abusive household who gets made homeless and all you've got is what's ahead of you. It's a really strong tone-setter imo, and I really like how much detail gets put into you scrounging around in the early game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535673#post1535673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's personal taste, I guess... I didn't like any of them. Usually with these sorts of setups where you have multiple companions and part of the story-structure is to pick them up, make them part of your &quot;squad&quot; and do &quot;Loyalty-missions&quot;, characters emerge that I find more likable than others but that weren't the situation here. I didn't like any of them. None of them seemed interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not much we can discuss there then. I really liked all of them, found them really fun and liked their dialogue, you didn't. Not much in the way of literary analysis there, I'd suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T14:41:48-07:00","id":1535678,"title":"","content":"1 - Having Gaia be dead would mean that everything would die and is the BSD take from prior editions that they use as an excuse to engage in foul self-indulgent behavior. They are explicitly noted as lying to themselves in W20 Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> 2 - Invoking the litany to eat a toxic-ass fomor is by far the dumbest ass usage of it I can think of, especially since that tenet is typically interpreted to mean &quot;loot goes to the boss&quot; or &quot;loot goes to the ones who can best make use of it&quot;. It depends on the Garou in question, they argued about how to use it frequently because it was open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> 3 - Younger Garou took issue with some tenets of the Litany. Probably not the &quot;Respect all those beneath ye- all are of Gaia&quot; or being ride or die for defending caerns. It's not an all or nothing deal.<br /> <br /> 4 - Elders still never had the stranglehold on Garou society that vampire elders did over vampire society (Garou elders tend to tangle directly with more threats and hence die with distressing frequency). The basic setup is still way too much of Vampire in Werewolf, especially with the trivialization of ancestor-spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T15:02:02-07:00","id":1535679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535675#post1535675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On launch. Don't remember my dialogue choice but I do remember getting that response.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so you got the choice as well in the launch-version, right? Try running the game again because it seems to me like one of the patches shortened that introduction-scenario. I mean, it's a good change in my opinion. The first time I played it I felt like that introduction was too long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree that's probably a good way to Homebrew it. But if if you're doing a pack-patron where everyone's getting the same general Favour and Ban, then it's not really &quot;unbalanced&quot; or anything, you're just putting stock into what your Chronicle is going to be about specifically. Everyone has the same access to it and is punished the same way, rather than things being all over the place. So homebrewing doesn't really have to worry about &quot;imbalance&quot; because every PC gets the same buff and punishment. </div> </div> </div>?<br /> <br /> But not everybody in a group is of the same Tribe....? The standard-process, as proposed by the book, is for individual PCs to pick their Tribe, so you're talking about a scenario where a homebrew replaces the corebook-rules, I guess. And at that point... I mean, sure, you can do that. I don't think it reflects well on that actual official release if that's supposed to be a &quot;solution&quot; but okay...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For one, younger Garou thinking the Litany is bullshit and that the Elders are talking nonsense (and are indeed part of the problem) isn't a W5 thing. It's an Apocalypse thing in general, and as far as I can tell has been a running theme for most of it. Likewise, the entire mood of older editions was saying that the Apocalypse is here, you're too late, and there's nothing you can do to avert it. This isn't a new addition to W5 either. I think W5 is actually <b>more</b> hopeful with it's tone by having Gaia be dead and the Apocalypse already ongoing or over, tbh. (A whole thing which I will probably have to put into it's own post.) </div> </div> </div>Well, you definitely have to put that in a longer post because here's the W5 definition of the Apocalypse:<br /> <br /> Apocalypse: The physical and spiritual end of the world, brought about by relentless human greed and consumption<br /> <br /> So, even according to W5 lore your post doesn't make sense. If it's ongoing, calling it more hopeful is ludicrous, if it has already happened then it doesn't make sense. Apocalypse is the literal end of all existence in WtA. There's nothing hopeful about something like that being an ongoing event and it's impossible for it to have already happened because we're talking about the end of everything in existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Garou having to relearn themselves is I think reflected pretty well in tone and showcased really well in BoHN. You're a creature of violence with a bubbling Rage underneath the surface, now try to make your community better and maintain your human connections. Like BoHN showcases this really well I think, with each Garou you meet being a weird iconoclast in some way shape or form. It's everyone scrounging to rebuild in the way they see fit in the midst of overwhelming trauma and grief. </div> </div> </div>I agree. This game is way better at setting up the W5 setting than the W5 corebook. Although I still think WtF has the better premise. The W5 premise is really complicated because part of it is e fallen Garou Nation. This thing that isn't present but its absence is part of why things are the way they are. I think that premise worked better when the Garou-Nation was a functioning but <i>very</i> flawed organization. &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; is such a good premise for WtF. W5's objective of unilaterally castigating Garou undermines the premise of the game rather than strengthens it. At that point, there's no need to even make the game about Garou. And yet that's the game.<br /> <br /> The game is doing good work in the sense that it actually provides an example of what W5 might be... that you don't get from the W5 corebook. It's one individual's interpretation of what W5 is aiming for. And we know it's this individual because Renegade with their supplements are heading in a different direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean it's establishing where you're starting from. You're a kid from an abusive household who gets made homeless and all you've got is what's ahead of you. It's a really strong tone-setter imo, and I really like how much detail gets put into you scrounging around in the early game. </div> </div> </div>Well, there are options here. What you describe is one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's not much we can discuss there then. I really liked all of them, found them really fun and liked their dialogue, you didn't. Not much in the way of literary analysis there, I'd suppose. </div> </div> </div>I mean, the reason I was vague was because of spoilers. As you know, you pick them up in their respective chapters and I didn't want to get into spoiler-territory for the game. But if you have a favorite companion and/or some line you want to mention that highlights why you like that character, feel free to present that.<br /> <br /> As I said, none of them piqued my interest. And their personalities weren't that interesting either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T15:07:18-07:00","id":1535681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535678#post1535678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Having Gaia be dead would mean that everything would die and is the BSD take from prior editions that they use as an excuse to engage in foul self-indulgent behavior. They are explicitly noted as lying to themselves in W20 Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> 2 - Invoking the litany to eat a toxic-ass fomor is by far the dumbest ass usage of it I can think of, especially since that tenet is typically interpreted to mean &quot;loot goes to the boss&quot; or &quot;loot goes to the ones who can best make use of it&quot;. It depends on the Garou in question, they argued about how to use it frequently because it was open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> 3 - Younger Garou took issue with some tenets of the Litany. Probably not the &quot;Respect all those beneath ye- all are of Gaia&quot; or being ride or die for defending caerns. It's not an all or nothing deal.<br /> <br /> 4 - Elders still never had the stranglehold on Garou society that vampire elders did over vampire society (Garou elders tend to tangle directly with more threats and hence die with distressing frequency). The basic setup is still way too much of Vampire in Werewolf, especially with the trivialization of ancestor-spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Or would it? The world has undergone 5 mass extinction events. If Gaia's so strong to survive those, how is she dying to Humanity? Maybe Gaia dying happens all the time, or the death of a God is just impossible to really make stick. That's why the Apocalypse is now completely different and I think it's more interesting as a result. The Wyrm isn't going to eat the entire world and render it defunct, but it is going to make <i>your</i> world worse. The BSD in this game even is a great example how someone spouting this kind of metaphysics at you sounds insane and blind to their current reality.<br /> <br /> 2. It's a silly interpretation of a silly tenant. It's open for interpretation and that's how Clay interprets it because no one in a 100 mile radius can tell him &quot;No&quot;. That's sorta a good showcase for why the Litany itself can be kinda silly.<br /> <br /> 3. I mean, yeah, but likewise they still had a problem with the Litany being a guidebook for the Garou nation. I played a character that tried to stick to the Litany to the best of his abilities, but was much more egalitarian and was down to ease up the Veil and introduce humans into the pack.<br /> <br /> 4. I mean yeah but that doesn't mean there wasn't a constant ideological clash. I also don't know what you mean by &quot;trivialize&quot; ancestor-spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T15:54:00-07:00","id":1535687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, so you got the choice as well in the launch-version, right? Try running the game again because it seems to me like one of the patches shortened that introduction-scenario. I mean, it's a good change in my opinion. The first time I played it I felt like that introduction was too long.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give it a looksie later.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">?<br /> <br /> But not everybody in a group is of the same Tribe....? The standard-process, as proposed by the book, is for individual PCs to pick their Tribe, so you're talking about a scenario where a homebrew replaces the corebook-rules, I guess. And at that point... I mean, sure, you can do that. I don't think it reflects well on that actual official release if that's supposed to be a &quot;solution&quot; but okay...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking specifically about the Rite of Patronage here. Since that's what we were talking about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you definitely have to put that in a longer post because here's the W5 definition of the Apocalypse:<br /> <br /> Apocalypse: The physical and spiritual end of the world, brought about by relentless human greed and consumption<br /> <br /> So, even according to W5 lore your post doesn't make sense. If it's ongoing, calling it more hopeful is ludicrous, if it has already happened then it doesn't make sense. Apocalypse is the literal end of all existence in WtA. There's nothing hopeful about something like that being an ongoing event and it's impossible for it to have already happened because we're talking about the end of everything in existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it ISN'T the end of everything in existence, just like how Climate Change ISN'T the end of the world despite the fact that it's already happening.<br /> <br /> The Apocalypse is allegorical for Climate Change in 5th edition. I don't think anyone can argue that. And in the real world, Climate Change is already a thing. You can't stop it because it's already happening. There's already rising sea levels and massive ecological disasters. <i>You </i>as a person aren't going to do dogshit in the face of that. What you <i>can</i> do and <i>should</i> do is work to help your local community and whatever charities you can devote the energy and resources to make the world a better place. And this is reflected in 5th. The Apocalypse is the destruction of everything you knew before, but the world's still <i>there</i>. You're still alive, you're still able to have fun, fall in love, laugh and have fun, help people, and make the world a better place. You can make your local environment better, be an activist that helps that mountain range or saves that endangered species. And the more people who do that, who make their world better, the more people can work to make their place better and so on to make the world better.<br /> <br /> That's the vibe of W5 now. You aren't going to save the world because no individual person can. No big furry Superman is going to come out of the blue and beat up the Wyrm and call it done. You're going to have to look at what's around you and make it better because you <i>should</i>. I personally find that a lot more engaging of a thesis especially with the removal of all of Werewolf's Omniprevelant Eugenics Lore making it much more of a willing fight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. This game is way better at setting up the W5 setting than the W5 corebook. Although I still think WtF has the better premise. The W5 premise is really complicated because part of it is e fallen Garou Nation. This thing that isn't present but its absence is part of why things are the way they are. I think that premise worked better when the Garou-Nation was a functioning but <i>very</i> flawed organization. &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; is such a good premise for WtF. W5's objective of unilaterally castigating Garou undermines the premise of the game rather than strengthens it. At that point, there's no need to even make the game about Garou. And yet that's the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree when the premise of W5 is now &quot;Post-Apocalypse&quot;. To use another piece of media as a vibe, it's like Fallout. The Old World isn't some grand utopia to return to, it's a failed state that caused the ruin of the world. That doesn't mean you should just wallow in the dirt for forever. It should just mean that's another chapter of history closed and it's time to learn from their mistakes and start anew.<br /> <br /> I also agree that WtF has the stronger premise! It's why I think W5 being closer to Forsaken than older Apocalypse in tone is why I'm enjoying it so much more than previous editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game is doing good work in the sense that it actually provides an example of what W5 might be... that you don't get from the W5 corebook. It's one individual's interpretation of what W5 is aiming for. And we know it's this individual because Renegade with their supplements are heading in a different direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we don't know that yet. Everyone assuming an immediate double-back on the reboot just because we have seen One Picture of Alberich are really jumping the gun I feel like.<br /> <br /> The book has the benefit of not having to make sweeping global statements. The reason a lot of characters can talk so assuredly is because things are true <i>as they believe them</i> but may in fact be factually incorrect in the grander scheme. During the game Elton's fairly certain there's less than a dozen werewolves in the entire tri-state area. I think personally, BoHN takes everything that's appealing about W5 and runs with it pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Also, of course the game is going to establish the setting better. It's 1.6 Million Words long. Kyle got a huge word budget to work with and W5 is about introducing a new baseline for other things to branch off of, not condensing 30 years of Deep Lore. The amount of information that needs to be relayed and the confines to do so are not remotely comparable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535679#post1535679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there are options here. What you describe is one of them.<br /> <br /> I mean, the reason I was vague was because of spoilers. As you know, you pick them up in their respective chapters and I didn't want to get into spoiler-territory for the game. But if you have a favorite companion and/or some line you want to mention that highlights why you like that character, feel free to present that.<br /> <br /> As I said, none of them piqued my interest. And their personalities weren't that interesting either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Elton: Someone dealing with grief but with a divine mandate to not show it is already a pretty strong premise even if it leans on the &quot;Wah me wife's dead&quot; trope a little bit, but he was a fantastic early mentor figure and later in the game as he begins to cut more and more loose with the rest of the pack was fun development. People thinking he's a weirdo for being a mundane occultist and relying on books is a fun trait, and as a Theurge character I was siding and relying on him quite a lot. He was a good introduction to the new vibe of Shadow Lords.<br /> <br /> Podge: Absolute riot of a character. Cannot imagine anyone seeing this scene and not enjoying him. <img title=\"HungryNames_G6Pu1j0aWA.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1542_1715812985442_954\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1542\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1542\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1542&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"HungryNames_G6Pu1j0aWA.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <img title=\"HungryNames_m5dFi9yxCe.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1544_1715814083894_304\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1544\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1544\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1544&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"HungryNames_m5dFi9yxCe.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b<br /> <br /> He was a constant warmonger, yeah, but\u200b the detail put into his tech-savvy and how the logic he put behind most of his violent actions made sense at the time was great.<br /> <br /> Nim: Incredibly fun. An amazing take on a Lupus-Born and the amount of care put into her musical references and behavior to make her enjoyable was something I was able to notice. She was a really fun take on a Galliard. I usually ended up siding with her when it came to things, since she vibed with what my character wanted to do more often than not.<br /> <br /> Melodie: Melodie has my absolute favorite line of dialogue in the game: &quot;I heard a little heresy once, from a friend who died before I was born.&quot; Her syncretism was an incredibly engaging worldbuilding tool and I really enjoyed what she brought to the table. I recruited her last and I'm sorta glad I did, since to me her recruitment quest seemed the most involved and fun to have everyone along with.<br /> <br /> I also think the Three Families are incredibly fun as a concept and that all of the characters introduced via them were rad. Staunch human supporter bannermen supporting their werewolf cousins any way they can is just cool to me.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the glimpses at the group chat were some of my favorite little bits in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","user":"Voytek","date":". 05-15-2024, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T16:54:53-07:00","id":1535693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535687#post1535687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm talking specifically about the Rite of Patronage here. Since that's what we were talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly! That's what I'm talking about as well! The rules-text for that Rite is a good indication of the limited vision and thoughtlessness in the W5 corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except it ISN'T the end of everything in existence </div> </div> </div>See, that's the core of the issue: You're wrong about that. In WtA (and that includes W5), the Apocalypse is the end of <i>everything</i>. That's it. They didn't do the &quot;Gehenna is a cycle&quot;-bit. The W5-Apocalypse is still the same-old world-ending event it was in previous editions. The only change is that W5 thinks that on one hand the Apocalypse is closer than ever and on the other hand, you can't prevent it. Or sometimes it does but there are more sections with a pessimistic tone in the book than an optimistic one. Occasionally the book contradicts itself in that regard. But the prevailing attitude is to be critical and pessimistic when it comes to Garou-activities.<br /> <br /> The take you outline isn't there in the W5 corebook. If anything, what the W5 corebook believes will happen is that Garou will make things worse most of the time no matter what they intend to do. And then there are the Fenrir and the BSD who actively work against the goals of the Garou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't agree when the premise of W5 is now &quot;Post-Apocalypse&quot;. To use another piece of media as a vibe, it's like Fallout. The Old World isn't some grand utopia to return to, it's a failed state that caused the ruin of the world. That doesn't mean you should just wallow in the dirt for forever. It should just mean that's another chapter of history closed and it's time to learn from their mistakes and start anew.<br /> <br /> I also agree that WtF has the stronger premise! It's why I think W5 being closer to Forsaken than older Apocalypse in tone is why I'm enjoying it so much more than previous editions. </div> </div> </div>No, I don't think W5 is post-Apocalypse as well but I also would point out that Fallout is a classic example of a post-Apocalypse-setting. So it's a bit puzzling to me what exactly your point is here...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, we don't know that yet. Everyone assuming an immediate double-back on the reboot just because we have seen One Picture of Alberich are really jumping the gun I feel like.<br /> <br /> The book has the benefit of not having to make sweeping global statements. The reason a lot of characters can talk so assuredly is because things are true <i>as they believe them</i> but may in fact be factually incorrect in the grander scheme. During the game Elton's fairly certain there's less than a dozen werewolves in the entire tri-state area. I think personally, BoHN takes everything that's appealing about W5 and runs with it pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Also, of course the game is going to establish the setting better. It's 1.6 Million Words long. Kyle got a huge word budget to work with and W5 is about introducing a new baseline for other things to branch off of, not condensing 30 years of Deep Lore. The amount of information that needs to be relayed and the confines to do so are not remotely comparable. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's doing better than the W5 corebook but it wasn't the wordcount that made the W5 corebook such a flawed corebook. Its misguided approach to lore was a far bigger issue. The whole &quot;who even knows&quot;-shrugging was a waste of space. So much wordcount wasted on just saying &quot;nobody knows&quot;. And then of course you had these hamfisted moments like the write-ups for the Auspices. All of them were superficial and each one got gradually worse with the Ahroun-write-up having an unserious description that ends with... &quot;Fuck you, Wyrm.&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure! </div> </div> </div>Just wanted to let you know that I saw that you tried to upload two images but they didn't. If you need help with posting them, just PM me. Because I do want to talk about the Garou you pick up in these chapters. But I assume those are screenshots of phone-conversations in the game...?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T17:26:16-07:00","id":1535696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535681#post1535681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Or would it? The world has undergone 5 mass extinction events. If Gaia's so strong to survive those, how is she dying to Humanity? Maybe Gaia dying happens all the time, or the death of a God is just impossible to really make stick. That's why the Apocalypse is now completely different and I think it's more interesting as a result. The Wyrm isn't going to eat the entire world and render it defunct, but it is going to make <i>your</i> world worse. The BSD in this game even is a great example how someone spouting this kind of metaphysics at you sounds insane and blind to their current reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mass extinction events, as terrible as they were, weren't the Apocalypse! They were, according to the Mokole, Wonder-Works of the Dissolver. The Apocalypse is far more... complete in its eradication, dissolution without rebirth. Also, tell me you didn't read at least The Last Battlefield scenario in Apocalypse without telling me you didn't read it; if you didn't manage to dislodge the hooks that the Wyrm was using to manifest on Gaia, the Wyrm devouring everything is, in fact, one of the things that's liable to happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. It's a silly interpretation of a silly tenant. It's open for interpretation and that's how Clay interprets it because no one in a 100 mile radius can tell him &quot;No&quot;. That's sorta a good showcase for why the Litany itself can be kinda silly. </div> </div> </div>Compounded with &quot;eat not the flesh of humans&quot;. Which is another one that younger Garou tended to not have a problem with because they were mostly human. Even Red Talons don't want to eat humans (they never want to see them ever again, really). Also, those who did partake of humans tended to wind up corrupt more often than not.<br /> <br /> That's not the litany being silly. Unlike that character, who didn't even have the excuse of botching a Wits roll after rolling 6+ successes to frenzy on Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. I mean, yeah, but likewise they still had a problem with the Litany being a guidebook for the Garou nation. I played a character that tried to stick to the Litany to the best of his abilities, but was much more egalitarian and was down to ease up the Veil and introduce humans into the pack. </div> </div> </div>As a lot of more modern Garou would be. But it's difficult to know that you can do this and it's actually endorsed by the game when it doesn't break down how most Garou feel about it, what the traditionalist and Ragabash standpoints on it are, what with W5 reducing it to a sidebar with no explanations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. I mean yeah but that doesn't mean there wasn't a constant ideological clash. I also don't know what you mean by &quot;trivialize&quot; ancestor-spirits. </div> </div> </div>Not having the Ancestors background and mentioning ancestor-spirits only in extreme passing is pretty noticeably trivializing them compared to prior editions. Also, younger Garou have a much shorter line to running things, though with the caveat that they, too, will probably die young, so trying to duplicate Vampire is the wrong way to approach this clash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-15T23:33:23-07:00","id":1535703,"title":"","content":"The Litany in W5 is missing two tenets, but otherwise is intact from Legacy.<br /> <br /> This means that Clay, as an experienced garou, should know VERY WELL that eating human flesh is forbidden, You shall not take an action that causes danger to caern and combat the Wyrm whever is dwells and wherever it breeds. If he doesn't then there are bigger problems with him than being an Elder. BSDs eat Fomors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T03:13:21-07:00","id":1535708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535703#post1535703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Litany in W5 is missing two tenets, but otherwise is intact from Legacy.<br /> <br /> This means that Clay, as an experienced garou, should know VERY WELL that eating human flesh is forbidden, You shall not take an action that causes danger to caern and combat the Wyrm whever is dwells and wherever it breeds. If he doesn't then there are bigger problems with him than being an Elder. BSDs eat Fomors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though the text is unclear, it could be that Clay only eats the horse....but as the horse is also fomori the question remains how a Garou who is so deeply incapable of rational thought ever got through their Rite of Passage let alone any further.<br /> <br /> Its very much part of the ' Elders suck' diatribe but it seems from Clays example that they also regularly snack on Tide Pods and play in traffic.....<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T04:37:56-07:00","id":1535711,"title":"","content":"The way it's written, Clay justifies it with &quot;The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station&quot;. I've never seen it interpreted before as a matter of &quot;Who gets to eat the enemy first?&quot;, like it's a point of pride to eat the enemy after a kill. And after you kill the horse-Fomori, it mentions that while it may not be human there is one part of the Litany that forbids you from eating humans. Though, so one option you can take is &quot;Damn the Litany! It has failed and now the world is all but lost. But I have won, so now I brush the flies away and eat.&quot;.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the whole setup with Scarper, Black Tarn and Clay is about the idea that &quot;Elders suck&quot;. Scarper and Clay act like bullies while Black Tarn, the Theurge, has some mental issues and isn't always lucid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T04:48:51-07:00","id":1535713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535711#post1535711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way it's written, Clay justifies it with &quot;The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station&quot;. I've never seen it interpreted before as a matter of &quot;Who gets to eat the enemy first?&quot;, like it's a point of pride to eat the enemy after a kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that the writer is thinking of classic werewolves and how THEY eat their victims. Because I see no reason for a garou to randomly munch on a fomori.<br /> <br /> Can you do that yourself? Eat an enemy you killed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T04:59:01-07:00","id":1535714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535713#post1535713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could be that the writer is thinking of classic werewolves and how THEY eat their victims. Because I see no reason for a garou to randomly munch on a fomori.<br /> <br /> Can you do that yourself? Eat an enemy you killed?</div> </div> </div> </div>As you try to eat, Clay comes and attacks you in Crinos Form. And then he snarls at you &quot;Have you forgotten the Litany?&quot; to which Scarper adds &quot;The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station&quot;. And then the options are:<ul><li>I've had enough of Clay's arrogance! He's old and I am victorious - I sink my teeth into his leg.</li> <li>&quot;Clay, maybe you shouldn't eat monster horse meat.&quot; It may be spiritually unclean.</li> <li>The Litany really is a farce, the &quot;ways of our people&quot; corrupt beyond worth. I back off and let him eat.</li> <li>We really are lost, if this is what we're reduced to - squabbling over scraps of power and meat. Clay is welcome to the sticky, sweet flesh. I back off.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T05:03:11-07:00","id":1535715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535714#post1535714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you try to eat, Clay comes and attacks you in Crinos Form. And then he snarls at you &quot;Have you forgotten the Litany?&quot; to which Scarper adds &quot;The First Share of the Kill for the Greatest in Station&quot;. And then the options are:<ul><li>I've had enough of Clay's arrogance! He's old and I am victorious - I sink my teeth into his leg.</li> <li>&quot;Clay, maybe you shouldn't eat monster horse meat.&quot; It may be spiritually unclean.</li> <li>The Litany really is a farce, the &quot;ways of our people&quot; corrupt beyond worth. I back off and let him eat.</li> <li>We really are lost, if this is what we're reduced to - squabbling over scraps of power and meat. Clay is welcome to the sticky, sweet flesh. I back off.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Does the PC, without our input, incite said scene?<br /> <br /> Can you ACTUALLY eat a foe later?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T05:09:15-07:00","id":1535716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535715#post1535715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does the PC, without our input, incite said scene?<br /> <br /> Can you ACTUALLY eat a foe later?</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not in that scene because the whole point of the scene is that Clay is the one who eats and that's what gets him sick which launches the whole story as your character is looking for help. But the text certainly suggests that Clay as an Elder Garou sees no problem with the idea of eating your foe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T05:13:42-07:00","id":1535717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535716#post1535716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Definitely not in that scene because the whole point of the scene is that Clay is the one who eats and that's what gets him sick which launches the whole story as your character is looking for help. But the text certainly suggests that Clay as an Elder Garou sees no problem with the idea of eating your foe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's freaking wild. But like, your PC WAS going to eat the horse if Clay hadn't pulled rank?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T06:11:39-07:00","id":1535720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535687#post1535687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except it ISN'T the end of everything in existence, just like how Climate Change ISN'T the end of the world despite the fact that it's already happening.<br /> <br /> The Apocalypse is allegorical for Climate Change in 5th edition. I don't think anyone can argue that. And in the real world, Climate Change is already a thing. You can't stop it because it's already happening. There's already rising sea levels and massive ecological disasters. <i>You </i>as a person aren't going to do dogshit in the face of that. What you <i>can</i> do and <i>should</i> do is work to help your local community and whatever charities you can devote the energy and resources to make the world a better place. And this is reflected in 5th. The Apocalypse is the destruction of everything you knew before, but the world's still <i>there</i>. You're still alive, you're still able to have fun, fall in love, laugh and have fun, help people, and make the world a better place. You can make your local environment better, be an activist that helps that mountain range or saves that endangered species. And the more people who do that, who make their world better, the more people can work to make their place better and so on to make the world better.<br /> <br /> That's the vibe of W5 now. You aren't going to save the world because no individual person can. No big furry Superman is going to come out of the blue and beat up the Wyrm and call it done. You're going to have to look at what's around you and make it better because you <i>should</i>. I personally find that a lot more engaging of a thesis especially with the removal of all of Werewolf's Omniprevelant Eugenics Lore making it much more of a willing fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Environmental destruction <i>to some extent</i> was already a foregone conclusion in Werewolf, and contrary to how it's often thought of, in older editions 'big furry Superman beating up the Wyrm and that being the end of it' wasn't in the cards. What was possible was saving Gaia and preventing the Wyrm and Weaver from killing or strangling everything. The real world analogue to that isn't &quot;climate change doesn't happen&quot; it's &quot;there is not a sixth mass extinction.&quot; And yes, that's still possible--we're in the opening stages of the sixth mass extinction now, but if environmental destruction was to cease, the extinctions that have already happened are not nearly severe enough to qualify what we've done for mass extinction status. To say that Gaia is already dead and all we can do is try to save a few shards is <i>really fucking convenient</i> for the people that don't want to avert the sixth mass extinction. There are plenty of those people--there's a whole cottage industry of people who state that nature/the wilds/Earth is dead, so we may as well scale back our efforts and only try to focus on small improvements to try and mitigate and adapt to a changing world.<br /> <br /> But they are wrong, and while the fight is dire it is not over yet. Resigning ourselves to it locks in the worst path. Not trying mass action and rejecting militancy--as W5's advocates frequently tell me it does--lock us into the worst path forwards too. And this line of thinking tends to be cowardly and self-centered--there are a lot of people who focus on global warming to the exclusion of all else because it can threaten them or their lifeways while habitat destruction or overexploitation doesn't. Many of these people are advocates of the &quot;mitigation and adaptation&quot; path and it's not uncommon for them to just breezily declare biodiversity loss a done deal. As even the social ecologists note on occasion, worrying about polar bears has become passe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T07:10:28-07:00","id":1535726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535717#post1535717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's freaking wild. But like, your PC WAS going to eat the horse if Clay hadn't pulled rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you would have. I also think another section from that part is what has led to this take about the Apocalypse not being that bad actually.<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"727\" height=\"823\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/5n7n7Cp.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5n7n7Cp.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/5n7n7Cp.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> But not even the W5 corebook goes that far as making a claim like &quot;The Apocalypse has come and gone.&quot;. Also in regards to WtA a setup like that would completely undermine the premise. What would even be the point anymore if the Apocalypse has happened but Garou are still running around now doing... what exactly? It would be like making the change in Vampire the Masquerade that in the new status quo actually quite a lot of people are completely aware of vampires being real, so the Masquerade has mostly been rendered unnecessary/ineffective. I don't really see the point in blowing up the premise to such a huge degree.<br /> <br /> Also, the talk about the Tribes implies that there are a lot more Tribes than there are in the lore, like how there are supposedly multiple Tribes that have fallen to the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T07:31:51-07:00","id":1535727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535726#post1535726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, you would have. I also think another section from that part is what has led to this take about the Apocalypse not being that bad actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, what? The text says Clay and buddies usually dispose of the corpses through pigs. The PC trying to eat it is a mistake Clay and co. are actively avoiding.<br /> <br /> Why'd he eat it just to wave his dick around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T07:46:55-07:00","id":1535728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535727#post1535727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, what? The text says Clay and buddies usually dispose of the corpses through pigs. The PC trying to eat it is a mistake Clay and co. are actively avoiding.<br /> <br /> Why'd he eat it just to wave his dick around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows... And then Clay is of course very insistent on him being the one who eats the horse monster. But it's also strange. Here in that screenshot it's set up that your character says &quot;Damn the Litany!&quot; and that's how they justify the decision to eat the monster. And yet as far as Clay is concerned, it's because he tries to uphold the Litany with &quot;The first share of the kill etc.&quot; that he explains why he decided to eat the horse monster. I guess, it tries to go for that idea from the W5 corebook that the Litany is always abused and only cynically used by Elders.<br /> <br /> But the whole eating-thing is weird anyway. When Clay is then falling sick, he gets no sympathy from me because I was immediately thinking &quot;I mean... what did you expect to happen here? You were eating a Fomor...&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T07:55:20-07:00","id":1535730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535728#post1535728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the whole eating-thing is weird anyway. When Clay is then falling sick, he gets no sympathy from me because I was immediately thinking &quot;I mean... what did you expect to happen here? You were eating a Fomor...&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also isn't rewarding to the player if a character acts like an idiot with no reason. If the pack was already tainted and invited the PC to munch, it'd be a good incentive for the player to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T10:24:09-07:00","id":1535738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1535717#post1535717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's freaking wild. But like, your PC WAS going to eat the horse if Clay hadn't pulled rank?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I can't help but think of DBZA. Eat that horse with me!... but only after I take a bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T15:15:05-07:00","id":1535752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocal