 05-21-2024, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T04:58:05-07:00","id":1536052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536031#post1536031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to shoehorn werewolves - or anything else, really, because it's probably the way of WoD5 - into a vampire setup seems like a terrible waste of potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's me explaining it poorly: the story structure and writing style are like Night Road, the setup and events are more werewolf. In fact there's a lot less pleasing your elders in my experience, although I managed to lose a whole dot of relationship for disagreeing with one's plan.<br /> <br /> See this is why my character is dating the cute enby! They don't throw a hissy fit just because I decide to try saving a barnful of humans (and failing because I only had five dots).<br /> <br /> It's not perfect, but it's not terrible. I personally highly enjoy it, but tolerances may vary.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>: I actually think the hunger rules are a better fit for rage, although I'd only include rage dice in stressful situations. Plus I might be weird for flicking back to the character sheet and relationships list a lot while playing these games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T06:55:15-07:00","id":1536055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536052#post1536052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>: I actually think the hunger rules are a better fit for rage, although I'd only include rage dice in stressful situations. Plus I might be weird for flicking back to the character sheet and relationships list a lot while playing these games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the problem with that is that you can satisfy hunger. Rage is bad both when empty AND when full.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T07:50:10-07:00","id":1536057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536055#post1536055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the problem with that is that you can satisfy hunger. Rage is bad both when empty AND when full.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a gameplay perspective? That's fine, and I'd argue better '0 Hunger=ideal'. Now you have a choice, do you keep your Rage low and risk not having power when you need it, or do you keep it high and risk it causing problems. It becomes an issue if players have very little control over their rage, but at it's core it's solid.<br /> <br /> Of course you could design the game around wildly varying rage, with werewolves swinging between heights of barely controlled power and horrific lows. But you'd probably want to reorient the rules so that every single roll can cause massive changes to the state of the game and story.<br /> <br /> Basically IMO the main mechanical issue is that they were building the game with the wrong tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T08:06:23-07:00","id":1536058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536057#post1536057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a gameplay perspective? That's fine, and I'd argue better '0 Hunger=ideal'. Now you have a choice, do you keep your Rage low and risk not having power when you need it, or do you keep it high and risk it causing problems. It becomes an issue if players have very little control over their rage, but at it's core it's solid.<br /> <br /> Of course you could design the game around wildly varying rage, with werewolves swinging between heights of barely controlled power and horrific lows. But you'd probably want to reorient the rules so that every single roll can cause massive changes to the state of the game and story.<br /> <br /> Basically IMO the main mechanical issue is that they were building the game with the wrong tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is the lack of player control that really ruins W5's Rage. That and the 'brilliant' idea to make Rage dice mandatory and so they all have to be used.<br /> <br /> And, still, the tiiny tiny pool XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T10:43:58-07:00","id":1536061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536058#post1536058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is the lack of player control that really ruins W5's Rage. That and the 'brilliant' idea to make Rage dice mandatory and so they all have to be used.<br /> <br /> And, still, the tiiny tiny pool XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what big teeth actually treats rage as a sliding bar that makes doing volient actions easier and non volient action harder. <br /> <br /> But that's kinda off topic for the thread...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:00:45-07:00","id":1536065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536061#post1536061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well what big teeth actually treats rage as a sliding bar that makes doing volient actions easier and non volient action harder.<br /> <br /> But that's kinda off topic for the thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean an anima banner-style counter for Rage that just acted like a paired Chi Condition from Weapons of the Gods to that same end would have been a lot simpler and left room for Essence/Gnosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-21T11:31:16-07:00","id":1536066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536061#post1536061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well what big teeth actually treats rage as a sliding bar that makes doing volient actions easier and non volient action harder.<br /> <br /> But that's kinda off topic for the thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think What Big Teeth serves as an excellent example of my issues. What Big Teeth is designed to be a depiction of the misery a minimum wage minority worker faces where the werewolf is a method of safely venting all that frustration. The game has mechanics for each type of wrong the characters face in their human lives.<br /> <br /> But Hungry Names? It has the job and the human stuff front and centre with very little point other than get money and fill up your Rage. The game isn't about the struggle like Big Teeth is, nevermind how it railroads you by making some big assumptions of what you'd do. Your PC is only complaining about freezing because they aren't allowed to shift to lupus, they cannot hunt their own food or just STEAL the things they need.<br /> <br /> Mind, none of this is bad writing, it is just focusing something that could be easily handwaved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-22T20:36:17-07:00","id":1536135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536066#post1536066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Hungry Names? It has the job and the human stuff front and centre with very little point other than get money and fill up your Rage. The game isn't about the struggle like Big Teeth is, nevermind how it railroads you by making some big assumptions of what you'd do. Your PC is only complaining about freezing because they aren't allowed to shift to lupus, they cannot hunt their own food or just STEAL the things they need.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be true at the very beginning of the story, but the job is mostly background noise during the majority of the game, until your boss becomes relevant to the story.<br /> <br /> The story forces you into a job because you end up spending years in Northampton. (The story takes place over at least two years, I think.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":387,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","user":"Caldorian","date":". 05-23-2024, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T03:21:46-07:00","id":1536147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caldorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536135#post1536135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may be true at the very beginning of the story, but the job is mostly background noise during the majority of the game, until your boss becomes relevant to the story.<br /> <br /> The story forces you into a job because you end up spending years in Northampton. (The story takes place over at least two years, I think.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I figured that's it. Mainly noting how there were solutions available that were not used.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, aside from the job and the heat bit, it is not bad. MUCH better than Earthblood, atleast XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T06:02:32-07:00","id":1536153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536065#post1536065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean an anima banner-style counter for Rage that just acted like a paired Chi Condition from Weapons of the Gods to that same end would have been a lot simpler and left room for Essence/Gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm it would would be intresting if you make a character using that system and run a adventure with them to see how quickly you can derail it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T10:56:18-07:00","id":1536159,"title":"","content":"So, you guys remember how we mused that the Rage system would make frenzying and taking crinos mean you lost the wolf? Yeah, friend had that happen in this game. So it IS true to the mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-23T16:02:55-07:00","id":1536171,"title":"","content":"On a somewhat related note a sequel to heart of the Forest is coming out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2463980/Werewolf_The_Apocalypse__Purgatory/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2463980/Werewolf_The_Apocalypse__Purgatory/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/2463980/Werewolf_The_Apocalypse__Purgatory/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.steampowered.com/app/2463980/Werewolf_The_Apocalypse__Purgatory/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T14:31:35-07:00","id":1536317,"title":"","content":"I am curious. Is Hauglosk featured in the game in any way and can it cripple your protagonist?<br /> <br /> Especially if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28297_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28297\" data-vbnamecard=\"28297\">Dehaka</a> would like to pitch in on this with their superior overview of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 05-26-2024, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T15:07:35-07:00","id":1536319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536317#post1536317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious. Is Hauglosk featured in the game in any way and can it cripple your protagonist?<br /> <br /> Especially if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28297_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28297\" data-vbnamecard=\"28297\">Dehaka</a> would like to pitch in on this with their superior overview of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far know no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T21:29:07-07:00","id":1536329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536317#post1536317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious. Is Hauglosk featured in the game in any way and can it cripple your protagonist?<br /> <br /> Especially if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28297_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28297\" data-vbnamecard=\"28297\">Dehaka</a> would like to pitch in on this with their superior overview of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I remember, the words &quot;Hauglosk&quot; or &quot;Harano&quot; aren't used directly at all, but there are somewhat frequent mentions towards the concepts of them. Things like (paraphrasing here since I'd have to go through again for direct quotes) &quot;The fugue that drains Garou of their will&quot; or &quot;Falling to the blind fanaticism that plagues the Cult&quot;. I wonder why there weren't any name-drops, since they are pretty important concepts for W5 core. But yes, even though I tried pretty hard on one of the playthroughs to be a murderhobo and fall some kind of way, all that came of that were chapter-skipping Frenzies, so I don't think it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka","name":"Dehaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28297_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:09:37-07:00","id":1536335,"title":"","content":"I thought it might be a bit hard to have a fulfilling narrative if it featured as the ticking timers presented in W5, thanks for clarifying<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28297_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28297\" data-vbnamecard=\"28297\">Dehaka</a> !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T04:45:36-07:00","id":1536338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536335#post1536335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it might be a bit hard to have a fulfilling narrative if it featured as the ticking timers presented in W5, thanks for clarifying<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28297_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28297\" data-vbnamecard=\"28297\">Dehaka</a> !</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the games don't have much influence on the RPGs, but I do ponder if Hauglosk/Harano get changed once it becomes clear they are antithetical to longer campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T05:12:55-07:00","id":1536420,"title":"","content":"From the looks of it, Heart of the Forest 2, though, has a Harano-tracker - but no Hauglosk-tracker.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's weird that Book of Hungry Names doesn't mention Hauglosk. In the Nim-chapter where you get your big confrontation with the Cult of Fenris, they never even talk about Hauglosk. Neither in the sense that all Cult-members are suffering from Hauglosk nor the idea that any Garou can fall prey to it. But if they keep doing the Nazi/extremist-bit with the Cult and every time they appear in a game or a supplement, they feel the need to add stuff like &quot;This Cult-member is also a white supremacist by the way.&quot; or like in Book of Hungry Names you make one of them a fan of this <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vegan_Reich\" target=\"_blank\">Vegan Reich</a> band, then &quot;falling to Hauglosk&quot; becomes a bit more of a queasy topic for any PCs in my opinion. I also don't like the idea that given that this is how the Cult is portrayed, an assumption is built that when the Cult shows up in W5 games, you gotta include this representation of right-wing extremist ideologies in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T06:52:03-07:00","id":1536424,"title":"","content":"It is a little odd to me that in his supposed extreme aversion to Nazi ideology Karim has mandated expressing it openly and fully in every piece of W5 media in ways it never was in Legacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T07:43:12-07:00","id":1536425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536420#post1536420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the looks of it, Heart of the Forest 2, though, has a Harano-tracker - but no Hauglosk-tracker.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's weird that Book of Hungry Names doesn't mention Hauglosk. In the Nim-chapter where you get your big confrontation with the Cult of Fenris, they never even talk about Hauglosk. Neither in the sense that all Cult-members are suffering from Hauglosk nor the idea that any Garou can fall prey to it. But if they keep doing the Nazi/extremist-bit with the Cult and every time they appear in a game or a supplement, they feel the need to add stuff like &quot;This Cult-member is also a white supremacist by the way.&quot; or like in Book of Hungry Names you make one of them a fan of this <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vegan_Reich\" target=\"_blank\">Vegan Reich</a> band, then &quot;falling to Hauglosk&quot; becomes a bit more of a queasy topic for any PCs in my opinion. I also don't like the idea that given that this is how the Cult is portrayed, an assumption is built that when the Cult shows up in W5 games, you gotta include this representation of right-wing extremist ideologies in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I prefer to see the Cult of Fenris as fanatics who will commit any atrocity in the name of Gaia rather than as Nazi-inspired white supremacists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T07:46:45-07:00","id":1536426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536425#post1536425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. I prefer to see the Cult of Fenris as fanatics who will commit any atrocity in the name of Gaia rather than as Nazi-inspired white supremacists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be difficult, since the orders from up top were to turn the Get into the Swords of Heimdall, and the marks left behind on this intention are quite deep. Also because as we've seen, it's very difficult for writers to go toward the &quot;did an atrocity&quot; without screaming off the edge of &quot;this just serves the Wyrm, you might as well have just used BSDs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T09:06:04-07:00","id":1536432,"title":"","content":"How the Cult was handled was one of the most frustrating things about this, made even worse by outside info like the behind-the-scenes stuff with Karim, or how they've been handled in other W5 supplements. When the character is first told about them, there's a very brief mention that &quot;They're not all white supremacists, but the ones we have around here are&quot; then proceed to refer to most of their idols, their spirits, the tribe at large, etc as some form of &quot;Nazi&quot; or &quot;fash&quot;, with the latter word or &quot;fascist&quot; being so overused in the book I thought I may have slipped into someone's social media ramblings whenever I was in a Cult section of the book. Barely-a-spoiler: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> You have the opportunity to call Ratatoskr a Nazi as one of the 'humorous' options.</div></div> </div> </div> It's also as if disproving the somewhat-joking, somewhat-serious sentiment from people seeing the Cult in the corebook and thinking they're the only ones being competent and fighting the Wyrm was mandatory. They're utterly incompetent here and don't even have Hauglosk to semi-excuse them, and (going into spoiler territory if people care) do such things as: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Starting a supervillain monologue about your pack's sudden but inevitable betrayal (then getting killed while monologuing), messing up a completely unrelated info-gathering mission of yours *that might help their goal* just because, working hand-in hand with the Wyrm instead of it being more like the Wyrm taking advantage of their blind hatred, revering an idol that reads 'Hitler' but not knowing it was of some female student with the same last name, </div></div> </div> </div> and so on. And as they are intertwined with the plot, these sort of things crop up often.<br /> <br /> You do get the opportunity to try to infiltrate them or work with them at some point, but it's not very well done even if you do it correctly. With the former, I had an <i>interesting</i> page that mentioned, &quot;It helps that you're white&quot; (as you can pick your char's ethnicity) while some random neo-nazi lady screamed slurs at my character to see if he was hip enough to be told about the Cult's plans, then giggled and let me in the know when he successfully didn't react. I really wish that there would be some W5-related media that doesn't just do the &quot;FASH&quot; thing with the Cult idea or just make them BSD-lite for some reason, and would actually provide some interesting scenarios about luring Garou with the promise of <i>doing something</i> when most of the Garou are bitter and moping about, instead of the Cult just being ridiculous villains. If there was any book that could have capitalized on the concept, it's this one, where most of the Garou are acting exactly that way when starting out. Instead, it's just making things somewhat uncomfortable, like Knightingale said, where falling to Hauglosk (or the general idea of being a fanatic since it's not name-dropped anywhere in this) automatically means you're white-supremacist or adjacent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka","name":"Dehaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28297_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T13:58:22-07:00","id":1536467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dehaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536432#post1536432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's also as if disproving the somewhat-joking, somewhat-serious sentiment from people seeing the Cult in the corebook and thinking they're the only ones being competent and fighting the Wyrm was mandatory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling it is something they focus on, given how basically every mention of them in W5 media doubles down on the fascism.<br /> <br /> I guess because not including it and making them even slightly competent would result in people asking why they are antagonists and not playable. Because they very much shot themselves in the foot by making the tribe/cult be defined by them fighting the foe first, which the book then spends time saying is wrong because reasons.<br /> <br /> But in doing this, W5 the more 'enlightened' edition has given neo-nazi more spotlight than indigenous people they were supposed to listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T14:06:10-07:00","id":1536468,"title":"","content":"Honestly I feel most nazi is projection on the writing part...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T14:20:26-07:00","id":1536469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536468#post1536468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I feel most nazi is projection on the writing part...</div> </div> </div> </div>We've had multiple authors now do this, so it might not be their choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T15:58:32-07:00","id":1536472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536469#post1536469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We've had multiple authors now do this, so it might not be their choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, or they give new writers a really, <i>really</i> bad primer on setting information that all of them are required to reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T19:05:20-07:00","id":1536477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536472#post1536472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That, or they give new writers a really, <i>really</i> bad primer on setting information that all of them are required to reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I mean, the writers are given directions to ensure the CoF never is anything more than a pathetic group of neo-nazi.<br /> <br /> But it isn't like BSDs are seeing any use, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T22:12:20-07:00","id":1536481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536477#post1536477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what I mean, the writers are given directions to ensure the CoF never is anything more than a pathetic group of neo-nazi.<br /> <br /> But it isn't like BSDs are seeing any use, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be far most modern media doesn't treat Fascists with any depth beyond simple Fascists Bad besides Mad Max: Fury Road and Disco Elysium.<br /> <br /> Fury Road to show with the absolute minimal amount of dialog how Immortan Joe's regime is a blight on the wasteland and make it clear with character like Nux that most of the warboys are victims that ol Joe regards less than the bullet farms's croups. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile Disco Elysium all of the fascist characters are treated as out of touch jokes who falls short of they espoused ideals but the story makes it clears that people who only adopted that belief as a coping mechanism to a world that moved on from they idealized version of the past. A character even states that Fascism is philosophy that's obsessed with turning back the clock to self destructive degrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T22:38:58-07:00","id":1536482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536481#post1536481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be far most modern media doesn't treat Fascists with any depth beyond simple Fascists Bad besides Mad Max: Fury Road and Disco Elysium.<br /> <br /> Fury Road to show with the absolute minimal amount of dialog how Immortan Joe's regime is a blight on the wasteland and make it clear with character like Nux that most of the warboys are victims that ol Joe regards less than the bullet farms's croups.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Disco Elysium all of the fascist characters are treated as out of touch jokes who falls short of they espoused ideals but the story makes it clears that people who only adopted that belief as a coping mechanism to a world that moved on from they idealized version of the past. A character even states that Fascism is philosophy that's obsessed with turning back the clock to self destructive degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference here is that you don't HAVE to make the CoF into fascists, they could be any other extremist. Yet the writing has doubled down on it hard.<br /> <br /> With the lack of Hauglosk in Hungry Names, the CoF seem less like a tribe and more like very foolish camp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T23:32:41-07:00","id":1536485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536482#post1536482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difference here is that you don't HAVE to make the CoF into fascists, they could be any other extremist. Yet the writing has doubled down on it hard.<br /> <br /> With the lack of Hauglosk in Hungry Names, the CoF seem less like a tribe and more like very foolish camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeh if the writing team insists on CoF being written as a fascists should add some nuance. Like take Nux from Fury Road for example. At the start of the movie he's a giddy supporter of Immortan Joe's regime and is totally content on dying from him yet despite that he's portrayed as a surprisingly emphatic person who's only loyal to Joe because that's only life he's ever known. As soon as Nux was shown kindness from one of Joe's runaway Bride he quickly develop doubts about his role in Joe's army (not helped by the fact that he <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BX-FMvt83fA\" target=\"_blank\">Fumbled Hard</a> during his attempt to capture Joe's Brides and immortal joe don't like Mediocres...) and go on to play a instrumental role to keep the war rig running and ending Immortan Joe's reign.<br /> <br /> Like the Cof in Book Of Hungry Names cold have a Nux type character who provided a more ground level view of the tribes philosophy and maybe a chance for the PC to redeem them. Especially when it's proven that the leaders actions is contrary with his own view on how a follower of Fenris should act...<br /> <br /> Of course I doubt that the current writing team have enough talent to do any of that. More like they have all the COF repeat the white howlers fuck up once they done with them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 05-29-2024, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T02:33:44-07:00","id":1536488,"title":"","content":"I think the W5 premise is just stumbling over itself in that regard. Because without the fascism-bit, you would have the Cult who say the other Garou are weak and they're the only true Garou around and then, well, the other Garou in question believe the Garou have fucked up, the Garou-Nation has fallen and Gaia's dead/dying. That doesn't feel like there's much of a disagreement there. But the Cult of Fenris at least has a take on the &quot;So now what?&quot;-question. Meanwhile, with the good Garou it's all a bit up in the air as to what the answer to &quot;So now what?&quot; actually is.<br /> <br /> It would all work better if there actually were some sort of alternative to the Cult, like &quot;The Cult thinks the Garou should do this but they're wrong because we should actually do this instead.&quot;. But what we've seen in the W5 works so far is that the good Garou reclaim caerns, deal with spirits, try to earn Renown, try to destroy Pentex-facilities or other kind of Wyrm-minion-holdouts... I mean, yeah, no shit, that's what Garou have already been doing in the past. It's not like the idea to hold and protect caerns, make pacts with spirits and try to take down Wyrm-stuff are grand revelations to Garou-kind. And yet according to the W5 premise this has gotten the Garou precisely nowhere. There's a finality to the failure of the Garou in W5 you didn't have before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T04:20:43-07:00","id":1536493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536488#post1536488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would all work better if there actually were some sort of alternative to the Cult, like &quot;The Cult thinks the Garou should do this but they're wrong because we should actually do this instead.&quot;. But what we've seen in the W5 works so far is that the good Garou reclaim caerns, deal with spirits, try to earn Renown, try to destroy Pentex-facilities or other kind of Wyrm-minion-holdouts... I mean, yeah, no shit, that's what Garou have already been doing in the past. It's not like the idea to hold and protect caerns, make pacts with spirits and try to take down Wyrm-stuff are grand revelations to Garou-kind. And yet according to the W5 premise this has gotten the Garou precisely nowhere. There's a finality to the failure of the Garou in W5 you didn't have before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at one of the ending for the good garou is releasing the ancestor sprits to guide the next generations. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T06:29:19-07:00","id":1536503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536493#post1536493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well at one of the ending for the good garou is releasing the ancestor sprits to guide the next generations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>...Which is exactly what W5 said is the problem in garou society, listening to the Old Ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T09:39:54-07:00","id":1536513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536493#post1536493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well at one of the ending for the good garou is releasing the ancestor sprits to guide the next generations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking more about the setting than having specific events like this in a game. And as pointed out, a part of the W5 premise is to say that the Garou have been a failure and that's why it's the Age of Apocalypse. So why would you consult the people who are responsible for the sad state of affairs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:28:39-07:00","id":1536525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536513#post1536513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking more about the setting than having specific events like this in a game. And as pointed out, a part of the W5 premise is to say that the Garou have been a failure and that's why it's the Age of Apocalypse. So why would you consult the people who are responsible for the sad state of affairs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well apparently those ancestors are totally benevolent and is really down to teaching the next generation so \ud83e\udd37.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T13:31:42-07:00","id":1536526,"title":"","content":"Whiplash is likely to be the order of the day, in terms of both our reactions and also how Renegade keeps telling the W5 core &quot;not quite my tempo&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T22:28:32-07:00","id":1536550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536526#post1536526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whiplash is likely to be the order of the day, in terms of both our reactions and also how Renegade keeps telling the W5 core &quot;not quite my tempo&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It feels like now that the dust had settled, that they realised W5's current state isn't really up to snuff XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T22:55:38-07:00","id":1536552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536526#post1536526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whiplash is likely to be the order of the day, in terms of both our reactions and also how Renegade keeps telling the W5 core &quot;not quite my tempo&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well apparently the ending involving the ancestor spirits involved a tiger sprit eating the cearn. So equivalent exchange I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T10:17:50-07:00","id":1536570,"title":"","content":"I'm going to have to buy the bloody corebook just so I properly understand all the complaints, aren't I?<br /> <br /> Honestly I have no issue with the Get being portrayed as fascists, although I still think they should be playable, but they should be <i>werewolf</i> fascists. They should care about whether a human is Kin rather than what ethnicity they are, and heck if the Garou Nation has fallen let's have them trying to reforge some half forgotten version of it. But now the Nation wasn't all bad, probably because someone realised that Garou needs to organise, so they can't exactly be doing that.<br /> <br /> You know I'd put money on any eventual W5 player's guide introducing a system where Hauglosk and Haruno are two ends of a scale, and make an implication that the CoF is what happens when you hit 7/5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T03:18:49-07:00","id":1536665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536570#post1536570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly I have no issue with the Get being portrayed as fascists, although I still think they should be playable, but they should be <i>werewolf</i> fascists. They should care about whether a human is Kin rather than what ethnicity they are, and heck if the Garou Nation has fallen let's have them trying to reforge some half forgotten version of it. But now the Nation wasn't all bad, probably because someone realised that Garou needs to organise, so they can't exactly be doing that.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know if I was in charge of writing the W5 player's guide I would actually make it clear that many werewolves would like to rebuild the garou nation or at least having a smaller system in place but most packs have very divegrent views on whaty the Garou Nation <i>is. </i> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-01T03:59:51-07:00","id":1536667,"title":"","content":"I think one way it could work is that the idea of &quot;The Garou Nation has fallen.&quot; is something you hear from BSDs, the Stargazers and the Fenrir. They each think they have a better idea of what to do with themselves. The BSD have completely abandonded the Garou-mission in favor of helping the Wyrm, the Fenrir believe they are the true Garou who will do things the right way now instead of the other Garou who have been too weak in the past and with the Stargazers you have Garou who still call themselves Garou but they think the strategy to deal with the bad state of the world should be wildly different. All those groups have an interest in calling the Garou-Nation fallen. Because it's not like the Garou Nation is some sort of modern nation-state and a fall is like the destruction of this state's bureaucracy or infrastructure or something. The Garou Nation is about having a common identity and common goals. So if anything what would make sense is for all the other Garou who also still call themselves Garou to be more like a loyalist faction. They still believe in the original mission, they still believe in Garou having a common identity and to them the Garou Nation is in crisis - but it isn't gone. They still believe that things can be turned around, and rebuilt and things can get better.<br /> <br /> The only way for the Garou-Nation to be truly fallen is if it's nothing but groups like the Fenrir and Stargazers: All these different groups with very different ideas of what to do but who also believe the original goals/strategies of the Garou-Nation have failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T02:35:24-07:00","id":1536693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1536667#post1536667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I suspect that half a dozen supplements from now the garou nation would be rebuild in the form bunch small networks of local Septs that may eventually aggregate into a few competing political blocs like in Werewolf the: Essentials. Assuming they don't write something extremely stupid like Gaia is behind the fall of the garou...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-05T17:23:27-07:00","id":1536854,"title":"","content":"So anyone has gone to the ancestor sprits ending? What's that about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-06T07:15:44-07:00","id":1536868,"title":"","content":"That ending was the first I got, so I don't remember every detail about it, but it was from doing the Ride the Tiger one. General spoilers for a couple of endings: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Basically, when you manage to successfully have the big bad Bane eat the caern but trick it so the true caern totem overpowers it, it sends a bunch of the ancestor-spirits of the caern scattering over the continent/world (can't remember which) while also saving the caern. There's some pages describing these spirits suddenly arriving to help other Garou via strange events, causing more Garou births, or hanging around to guide them in the fight against the Wyrm. It's about as close to making a greater difference outside of your caern as it gets, as in another ending, the caern was saved, but the most that happens outside of the caern is your character's pack sharing what they know about the big bad BSD's plot to other Garou so they're prepared in case someone tries it again. In any ending, you can pick a 'The Adventures Continue...' choice about what your character does in the months to come, like if you were human-focused, it notes that you spend time shoring up relations and repairing the nearby town. Other ones were like 'Continue to share what you know' or 'Keep taking the fight to the Wyrm'.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think the ancestors ending was fine enough to try and make there be a greater impact on the fight against the Wyrm, even with the sometimes-confusing ways spirits work in this book. It's still a bit vague as to how much impact those events will have in the long run, but it's an attempt. The other ending was pretty 'keep-to-your-caern' in nature, though. I didn't finish a third playthrough to see what would happen if you <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> let the caern and totem get destroyed to beat the BSD, </div></div> </div> </div> in case that forces the character's pack to try and make a difference somewhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28297-dehaka","name":"Dehaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28297_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:58:59-07:00","id":1537008,"title":"","content":"Ok, as someone who gave up after multiple resets........why is Answering Tiger Answering Tiger? I mean the spirit acts like a slightly more stable Nexus Crawler....but why the Tiger imagery in Massachusetts? Stormcat is also an odd one considering the lack of strong Puma folkloric or mythological footprints in the region with most of the storm aspected spirits being avian such as Wind or Thunderbirds.<br /> <br /> Horned Serpent should be fairly strong in the region with links to Chipi/Hobomock, but the GC are essentially absent.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:18:31-07:00","id":1537021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1535340-w5-videogame-text-adventure-book-of-hungry-names-review-first-impressions?p=1537008#post1537008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, as someone who gave up after multiple resets........why is Answering Tiger Answering Tiger? I mean the spirit acts like a slightly more stable Nexus Crawler....but why the Tiger imagery in Massachusetts? Stormcat is also an odd one considering the lack of strong Puma folkloric or mythological footprints in the region with most of the storm aspected spirits being avian such as Wind or Thunderbirds.<br /> <br /> Horned Serpent should be fairly strong in the region with links to Chipi/Hobomock, but the GC are essentially absent.....</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing W5, they'd make anything puma-related involve a magic belt that makes you fall at 60 degrees, breaking all known laws of physics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}